# Synapse ↔ PM integration

Before changing SSO or PM HTTP calls, read [docs/PM_API_CONTRACT.md](../../docs/PM_API_CONTRACT.md).

## Direction of data

| Flow | Owner | Mechanism |
|------|-------|-----------|
| Auth | PM issues access token via SSO | `/sso/authorize` + `/api/sso/token` |
| Create/link project | Synapse → PM | `POST /api/projects` |
| Push checkbox → task | Synapse → PM | `POST /api/tasks` (+ Synapse* fields) |
| Toggle done | Synapse → PM | `PUT /api/tasks/:id` `{ status }` |
| PM task closed elsewhere | Synapse pulls | `GET /api/tasks/project/:id` then update markdown |
| Open task in PM | Deep link | `/projects/{id}?tab=tasks&taskId={id}` |
| Open note from PM | Deep link | `/vaults/{id}?note={noteId}` |

## Rules

- Never assume PM will call Synapse.
- Store PM access token encrypted in `SsoTokens`; treat 401 as re-auth.
- When adding a PM API dependency, update `PM_API_CONTRACT.md` and `pmClient.ts` together.
- Task create should send `synapseVaultId`, `synapseNoteId`, `synapseMarkerId`, `synapseNoteUrl` so PM can show “Open in Synapse” only when linked.
